From e819d4189db95743f8a68ae83d8dff73e88e08a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:00:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mm/nommu: check sharing only when a direct mapping
 succeeded
To: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>,
    "Liam R. Howlett" <liam@infradead.org>,
    Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@kernel.org>,
    David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>,
    Jann Horn <jannh@google.com>,
    Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>,
    Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>,
    Greg Ungerer <gerg@linux-m68k.org>,
    linux-mm@kvack.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

When the mmap capabilities of a file include NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT,
do_mmap_private() calls the file's mmap hook, and makes a private copy
instead if the hook returns -ENOSYS. Commit b6b7a8faf05c ("mm/nommu:
don't use VM_MAYSHARE for MAP_PRIVATE mappings") turned the BUG_ON()
that checked a successful direct mapping for sharing into a
WARN_ON_ONCE() that runs whatever the hook returned. A mapping for which
the hook returned an error is not shared, so the fallback path, which is
legitimate, now triggers the warning.

That path is taken for a read-only MAP_PRIVATE mapping of a ramfs file
made by a ptraced process: VM_MAYOVERLAY is not set on such a mapping,
so that breakpoints can be written into it, ramfs_nommu_mmap_prepare()
returns -ENOSYS, and a private copy is made. Starting a program from
ramfs under a debugger therefore produces:

  WARNING: mm/nommu.c:932 at do_mmap+0x4e0/0x73c

Check for sharing only when the hook succeeded. The BUG_ON() before that
commit was inside the success branch.

Reproduced on QEMU's riscv64 virt machine with nommu_virt_defconfig: a
child calls ptrace(PTRACE_TRACEME) and maps a file of the initramfs
read-only and private. The mapping succeeds with or without this patch;
the warning only appears without it.

Fixes: b6b7a8faf05c ("mm/nommu: don't use VM_MAYSHARE for MAP_PRIVATE mappings")
Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
---
 mm/nommu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/nommu.c b/mm/nommu.c
index 605cc4021a..ffa0c88c8e 100644
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -932,7 +932,7 @@ static int do_mmap_private(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 	if (capabilities & NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT) {
 		ret = mmap_file(vma->vm_file, vma);
 		/* shouldn't return success if we're not sharing */
-		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(!is_nommu_shared_mapping(vma->vm_flags)))
+		if (!ret && WARN_ON_ONCE(!is_nommu_shared_mapping(vma->vm_flags)))
 			ret = -ENOSYS;
 		if (ret == 0) {
 			vma->vm_region->vm_top = vma->vm_region->vm_end;
-- 
2.47.3

